<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Empress Dugu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">544–602</span> · <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a> · Also known as Dugu Qieluo, Empress Wenxian</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Empress Dugu (Dugu Qieluo) was the wife of Emperor Wen, founder of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sui-dynasty">Sui dynasty</a>, and a daughter of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/xianbei">Xianbei</a> general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dugu-xin">Dugu Xin</a>. She had great influence over state affairs, insisted that her husband take no concubines and helped persuade him to replace the crown prince Yang Yong with Yang <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guan-people">Guang</a>, the future <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emperor-yang-of-sui">Emperor Yang</a>. She was posthumously honoured as Empress Wenxian.</p></div>
